<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Fleet.Contracts</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    What one fleet service puts on the broker or sends over HTTP for another: message records,
    message type and gate names, exchange and queue names with their arguments, and the journal
    token format. One declaration, used by the producer and the consumer.

    MUST NOT add a PackageReference or a ProjectReference. Every service references this project,
    the secret forwarder's neighbours included, so a dependency added here ships in all of them.
    ContractsProjectDependencyTests (tests/Fleet.Protocol.Tests) fails on one.

    Not Fleet.Protocol: that is the versioned conversation protocol a client outside the fleet can
    implement. These are internal shapes with no version, changed only together with the samples
    under tests/fixtures/wire, and a client has no use for them.
  -->

</Project>
